{"chunk_id": "1339d5cd1dd0", "text": "Tensions briefly flare among the Pandava allies when Satyaki and the Panchala prince nearly clash, but Sahadeva, Krishna, and Yudhishthira intervene and restore unity just as the larger battle resumes. The focus then shifts to Ashwatthaman, son of Drona, who unleashes devastating fury on the battlefield. After creating a gruesome carnage described as a mountain of the dead, he vows revenge for the deceptive killing of his father and calls on Duryodhana to rally the Kaurava army. Ashwatthaman then invokes the terrible Narayana weapon, filling the sky with blazing arrows, discs, maces, and iron missiles that devastate the Pandava forces. Overwhelmed and terrified, Yudhishthira momentarily loses hope, reflecting bitterly on Drona\u2019s death and the moral cost of the war as his army begins to break under the weapon\u2019s unstoppable power.\nAswatthaman unleashes the Narayana weapon after vowing revenge for Drona, devastating the Pandava army and terrifying Yudhishthira.\nThemes: vengeance for Drona, divine weapons, battle carnage, despair of Yudhishthira, escalation of war", "vector": [-0.02166142873466015, -0.015688208863139153, 0.006663747131824493, 0.017552288249135017, -0.00013776506239082664, 0.019797349348664284, -0.03153969347476959, -0.01472215261310339, -0.01555214449763298, -0.003823405597358942, 0.020777011290192604, 0.012987333349883556, 0.01156546175479889, 0.018654409795999527, 0.016871968284249306, 0.0029559959657490253, 0.03959469869732857, -0.01006875466555357, 0.015701815485954285, -0.02137569524347782, -0.00970138143748045, -0.004728232976049185, -0.0009635050082579255, 0.033390168100595474, -0.013021348975598812, 0.02639646641910076, 0.0038744297344237566, -0.03012462705373764, 0.013558803126215935, -0.006585509981960058, -0.010184410028159618, -0.0057112970389425755, 0.008286313153803349, 0.0059289997443556786, -0.024641236290335655, 0.0013172720791772008, -0.0034407249186187983, -0.018504738807678223, 0.0068